WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.293
- Well, I was going to
ask you about your kids.

00:00:02.293 --> 00:00:03.646
But everybody always
asks about kids first.

00:00:03.646 --> 00:00:04.592
How are you?

00:00:04.592 --> 00:00:08.675
- Oh. I'm okay. I was so
happy to leave my house.

00:00:10.489 --> 00:00:15.239
I was so happy to leave. Just
my room, and my other room,

00:00:16.287 --> 00:00:19.963
and the kids. Where are you
going, mom? Where are you going?

00:00:19.963 --> 00:00:20.796
- Away.

00:00:20.796 --> 00:00:21.629
- Away.

00:00:21.629 --> 00:00:22.462
- Yeah.

00:00:22.462 --> 00:00:24.358
- Far, far away. To Burbank.

00:00:24.358 --> 00:00:27.366
- To Burbank. It's been
a lot though, especially

00:00:27.366 --> 00:00:30.025
a mom that's just trapped home
with their kids, it's a lot.

00:00:30.025 --> 00:00:33.465
- I'm trapped home with my
kids, I hide a lot, they

00:00:33.465 --> 00:00:37.553
find me in the pantry,
they find me in my closet,

00:00:37.553 --> 00:00:39.825
they find me eating and drinking,

00:00:39.825 --> 00:00:40.658
- Yep.

00:00:40.658 --> 00:00:43.060
- They find me, literally,
they can find me.

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:44.856
And I have quite a big
house, I'm not gonna lie.

00:00:44.856 --> 00:00:45.689
- Yep.

00:00:45.689 --> 00:00:46.522
- And they find me.
- They find you.

00:00:46.522 --> 00:00:47.380
- Mhm.
- They sense it.

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:51.026
- The other day I was talking
to my girlfriend, and she was,

00:00:51.026 --> 00:00:53.301
we were, I don't even know, just talking.

00:00:53.301 --> 00:00:56.382
I was like behind a chair in my room,

00:00:56.382 --> 00:01:00.301
like, in like, you know,
criss-cross freaking applesauce,

00:01:00.301 --> 00:01:01.774
like, and I'm like, and they're like,

00:01:01.774 --> 00:01:02.607
what are you doing?

00:01:02.607 --> 00:01:06.245
And I'm like, I'm in my
own Mommy fort. So, anyway.

00:01:06.245 --> 00:01:08.034
- All my kids do are, they make forts.

00:01:08.034 --> 00:01:09.391
- Oh, we made a fort this morning.

00:01:09.391 --> 00:01:11.690
Before we left for school.
- Oh it's every time.

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:13.028
The only reason why there's not is because

00:01:13.028 --> 00:01:14.773
I threw a Neverland party
for my kids so there's like

00:01:14.773 --> 00:01:16.741
teepees and stuff so they're
not like...but usually

00:01:16.741 --> 00:01:19.237
every day is a fort. I'm like,
can we build something else?

00:01:19.237 --> 00:01:21.362
Can we call it a castle?
Can we call it, you know,

00:01:21.362 --> 00:01:22.527
something, a tree house?

00:01:22.527 --> 00:01:23.392
- Can we call it anything else?

00:01:23.392 --> 00:01:24.225
- Anything else.

00:01:24.225 --> 00:01:25.677
- No but we have forts,
we have forts upstairs

00:01:25.677 --> 00:01:28.258
